{
  "name": "horsefly",
  "_about": "A horsefly -- the band-eyed horsefly (Tabanus bovinus), 22 mm long: stout and broad; a wide head that is almost all eye, big green-bronze eyes crossed by shining purple bands; short stout antennae jutting forward; blade-like biting mouthparts hanging below; a brownish-grey, finely haired thorax; a broad flat abdomen, brown, with a pale triangle on the midline of each ring and pale patches at the sides; clear, faintly smoky wings held out flat in a delta at rest. Coat: the cleg (Haematopota, grey, the wings mottled). Written whole by tools/creaturegen/rework/winged/flies.py on insectlib.py + wlib.py (jointed legs on a walking gait; the wings at rest laid back over the abdomen, swung out and beating in the variant \"flying\").",
